      "fetchDaily": false,
      "riteData": {
        "EN": {
          "holy_saturday_rest": {
            "lines": [
              {
                "sp": "",
                "text": "<HOLY SATURDAY"
              },
              {
                "sp": "",
                "text": "1. On Holy Saturday the Church waits at the Lord’s tomb in prayer and fasting, meditating on"
              },
              {
                "sp": "",
                "text": "his Passion and Death and on his Descent into Hell, and awaiting his Resurrection."
              },
              {
                "sp": "",
                "text": "2. The Church abstains from the Sacrifice of the Mass, with the sacred table left bare, until after"
              },
              {
                "sp": "",
                "text": "the solemn Vigil, that is, the anticipation by night of the Resurrection, when the time comes"
              },
              {
                "sp": "",
                "text": "for paschal joys, the abundance of which overflows to occupy fifty days."
              },
              {
                "sp": "",
                "text": "3. Holy Communion may only be given on this day as Viaticum.>"
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      },
      "data": {
        "EN": {}
      },
